<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-2">2 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">NASA's Stardust probe flies through the tail of comet Wild 2</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Stardust passed within about 240 km of comet Wild 2's nucleus, collecting dust in blocks of aerogel. The samples, returned to Earth in 2006, were the first material ever brought back from a comet.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-3">3 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">NASA's Spirit rover lands in Mars's Gusev Crater</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Cushioned by airbags, Spirit bounced to a halt on Mars on the evening of 3 January, US time. Planned to last 90 days, it explored for over six years and found evidence of past water.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-4">4 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mark Zuckerberg launches 'TheFacebook' at Harvard</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Harvard student launched a social network for fellow students. Opened to the public in 2006, Facebook grew to billions of users and transformed how people share news and personal life.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-26">26 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake and tsunami devastate the Indian Ocean</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 9.1 earthquake off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a> sent tsunamis across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, killing about 230,000 people in 14 countries. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> were worst hit.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/2004-summer-olympics" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/2004-summer-olympics.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/2004-summer-olympics">2004 Summer Olympics</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 2004 Summer Olympics were held in Athens from 13 to 29 August 2004, bringing the Games back to the city of the first modern Olympics of 1896.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-ivan" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hurricane-ivan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-ivan">Hurricane Ivan</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Hurricane Ivan was a powerful Atlantic hurricane that struck the Caribbean and the United States in September 2004.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/2004-indian-ocean-earthquake-and-tsunami" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/2004-indian-ocean-earthquake-and-tsunami.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/2004-indian-ocean-earthquake-and-tsunami">2004 Indian Ocean earthquake and tsunami</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The 2004 Indian Ocean earthquake and tsunami began on 26 December 2004, when an undersea megathrust earthquake of magnitude 9.2–9.3 struck off the west coast of Aceh in northern Sumatra, Indonesia, along the boundary between the Burma plate and the Indian…</p></div></li></ol></section>
